Z||000000||billfredmike24||08-15-2001||03:35 PM||||I just installed a pioneer cd deck and everything works fine.....except i have a grey wire remaining.  The original plugs were all cut off by p/o so i had to wire them individually.  There were two grey wires, one for one of the speakers, and now i have this loose one??? Anyone know what it's for???  <BR>Thanks Mike<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_10.jpg"> <BR>yeah the wheels are ugly, and the stickers, that'll change||||reg||1
Z||000001||mbramble||08-15-2001||04:15 PM||||It's probably for the backlighting that is controlled by the interior dimmer switch.||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||08-15-2001||04:16 PM||||Grey is the front set, grey/blk and grey  front left actually||||reg||1
Z||000003||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-15-2001||04:29 PM||||Hopefully this will be help to you.<P>(Sorry for the size but I left it large so you can read it when its printed)<P><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/radiowiring.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by isthiswhereiputausername? (edited 08-15-2001).]||||reg||1
