Z||000009||billfredmike24||08-15-2001||10:22 PM||||Call me an idiot but i don't ever recall dimming my lights, how do i do this?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||fierohoho||08-15-2001||10:31 PM||||Any time I see a Fiero in the junk yard with the factory radio plugs still in it I pull em. I've replaced those plugs in all three of my cars. Now I just buy the adaptor plugs for a retrofit application. If I decide to sell the car its a 10 minute job to put the old radio back in. Just my 2/100 of a dollar <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000011||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-15-2001||10:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierohoho:<BR><B>Any time I see a Fiero in the junk yard with the factory radio plugs still in it I pull em. I've replaced those plugs in all three of my cars. Now I just buy the adaptor plugs for a retrofit application. If I decide to sell the car its a 10 minute job to put the old radio back in. Just my 2/100 of a dollar  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Great idea Fierohoho! <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||billfredmike24||08-16-2001||12:28 AM||||fierohoho: i've checked about five fieros in local yards and none had the wiring harness, even the parts car i bought didn't have it.  Anybody got any radio mounting brackets they could sell me?||||reg||1
Z||000013||mbramble||08-16-2001||07:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by billfredmike24:<BR><B>Call me an idiot but i don't ever recall dimming my lights, how do i do this?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The stock radios have a 'panel light' (see above drawing) that is dimmable with the rotary dimmer switch below the headlight switch.  Dims the same as the lights in the instrument panel and the one in the AC/heater control head.  The wire that feeds it is gray.  In the stock units this panel light bulb shines red (just like in the instrument panel) to illuminate the lettering for the controls.<P>There is also a brown wire listed as the 'display dim signal' in the drawing above. This is for when the headlights are turned on -- the display (digital clock, etc.) will dim when your lights have been turned on, brighten when they are turned off.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||fierohoho||08-16-2001||11:14 AM||||I have a set of spare plugs if you want them, I'll check for the mounts.<P>Would this be for a factory radio or after market?<P>I took an after market radio out of my '86 and have the adapter from that, I bet you could get that at Wally World pretty cheap though.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000015||billfredmike24||08-16-2001||12:12 PM||||Thanks Mr. Ramble<P>fierohoho- i'll check some more around here but if you find any mounts and the clips that hold em on that would be great.<BR>Thanks Mike ||||reg||1
